.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-08-29 a
.Cm cancel
piped into
.Xr head 1
was killed part-way, and the pool was left with no
.Ql bootfs ;
it now ignores a closed output.
On 2026-08-30 a bare
.Nm rollback
with no terminal rolled back and restarted the machine.
On 2026-08-26 it reported the Secure Boot path on machines booting
through ZFSBootMenu.
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page:
.Cm list
cut snapshot names at 34 characters, so sanoid's weekly and monthly
names were shown short and refused by
.Cm to ;
.Cm status
run as a user, who cannot read the EFI system partition, died with
.Dq FAIL at line 953 ;
and every command acted on the alphabetically first pool imported, not
the running one \(em shown with a throwaway pool named to sort first.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The clone depends on its origin snapshot, so the old environment cannot
be destroyed while the clone exists;
.Xr zfs-promote 8
reverses that once the rollback is settled.
.Pp
The machine starts from the snapshot's files but the pool's other
datasets as they are now: a service whose data moved on since, a
database's for one, meets data newer than itself.
